5682672420107_n.png?_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=wd2lzFe87vUQ7kNvwGmbEAA&_nc_oc=AdpWYSCjNfOcNId9XaRJzXqZYlj4925tMk617EGPYPG5cOPKBIooA1nO708XRefW73Q&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-atl3-1.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_Af2pKybIfurXmqWw43TzNcjTIPcCXeh7vKuEDR4SgfaWIA&oe=69F21357"}, "display_name": "PROM Simulator (Shoulder Care)", "keywords": ["CNA", "nurse", "nursing", "Shoulder", "training"], "long_description": "In this VR Simulation, learners will master the essential skill of performing passive range of motion (PROM) exercises for a patient's shoulder, focusing on maintaining flexibility and preventing stiffness. \n\nWith multi-language support (English, Spanish, French, and Arabic), this simulator ensures inclusivity and accessibility for a global audience.  \n\nThe experience is enhanced by an AI companion, acting as a virtual mentor, to answer questions to reinforce learning.\n \n# Key Features: \n- Multi-Language Support: Tailored instructions and narrations in four major languages to cater to diverse learners. \n- AI Companion: An interactive assistant that responds to user queries, and provides clarifications to meet learning needs.(NOTE: Generative AI is still experimental)\n\n\n# Learning Objectives:\n- Remember the steps and protocols for performing PROM exercises.\n- Understand the importance of maintaining joint flexibility and preventing stiffness.\n- Apply the correct techniques to perform PROM exercises safely.\n- Analyze the patient's response to the exercises to ensure comfort.\n- Evaluate their own technique to ensure it adheres to best practices and safety standards.\n- Create a supportive and effective exercise environment for patients through proper PROM techniques.\n\nThis comprehensive approach ensures CNAs are well-prepared to assist patients with \nproper care efficiently and compassionately in real-world clinical settings", "short_description": "Learn to perform passive range of motion exercises for a patient's \nshoulder to maintain flexibili